{
  "title": "Malformed parenthetical fragments still survive ingredient parsing",
  "description": "The plus/unit cleanup in \
`p4-ingredient-parser-residual-plus-and-paren-edge-cases` fixed the safe \
measurement cases, but the genuinely malformed parenthetical source fragments \
still remain in `data/unique-ingredients.txt` after the 2026-07-06 pipeline \
rerun:\n\
\n\
- `(16-ounce can chickpeas` from a source line with no closing parenthesis.\n\
- `(440-gram) cans`, where the preceding line is already parenthesis-balanced \
and the continuation heuristic has no safe signal to merge it.\n\
- `(about 3 to 3 1/2 ouncesgrated Parmesan cheese`, from a source typo with a \
missing space and missing closing parenthesis.\n\
\n\
These need a separate, intentionally narrow parser/extraction pass. Avoid a \
broad leading-`(` merge heuristic unless it is pinned with fixtures and a \
`make pipeline` diff proving it does not merge unrelated ingredients.",
